#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ArchangeSDR: sweeps frequency ranges with an RTL-SDR dongle and reports those where someone is
talking (and, on FM radio, the stations that are on the air).

    archangesdr [--profile P]                GTK window (scan, detection log, statistics, settings)
    archangesdr --cli 144-146 [--passes N]   same detection in the terminal (tests, tuning)
    archangesdr --bands                      configured ranges

The program was called SDRScanner: `sdrscanner` stays a command for it (the desktops' menus call it) and
its standalone folders move to the new name at the first start.

Profiles (--profile, ARCHANGESDR_PROFILE, else detected) keep the files of the desktop it runs in:
    ubonsole    uBonsole (i3, uConsole): ~/.config/i3/ubonsole.conf, ranges ~/.config/i3/scanner-ranges.json,
                defaults from ~/.config/i3/frequencies/<region>/<lang>.json, data ~/.local/share/ubonsole
    archsdr     archSDR (Hyprland): ~/.config/radio-menu/radio.conf, ranges
                ~/.config/radio-menu/scanner-ranges.json, data ~/.local/share/radio-menu
    standalone  ~/.config/archangesdr/archangesdr.conf, ranges ~/.config/archangesdr/ranges.json,
                data ~/.local/share/archangesdr
Settings in that file (bash KEY=value): SDR_DEVICE (index or serial), SDR_GAIN (dB), the language
(UBONSOLE_LANG, RADIO_LANG or SCANNER_LANG: en, fr, de, es), the region (UBONSOLE_REGION, RADIO_REGION
or SCANNER_REGION: a folder of ranges/: eu, fr, uk, de, es, us, ca, br, ar, cl, co, sa, jp, cn, ru, au)
and, under Hyprland, RADIO_WS (workspace GQRX opens on).

Ranges are editable in the app; the first start copies the defaults of the region and language (the
voice ranges of the region's frequency sheet, AM, NFM, FM, USB, LSB, and FM radio; never the "do not
listen" ranges), from the desktop's own files when it has them, else from ranges/ next to the program.

Two-step sweep: survey in 2.06 MHz hops (0.1 s each, 90 % of the width the dongle captures), then a
progressive listen (1 to 2.5 s, as soon as the verdict is clear) only where a narrow peak showed up; a
finished conversation is checked again every 8 s for 90 s (the reply). A frequency is "active" when the signal lasts
long enough AND its demodulation looks like speech (syllables, pauses, energy in 300 - 3000 Hz, voiced
frames). Rejected: continuous carriers, broadband interference, short pulses, wide signals, digital
data and tones; what was listened to without speech is muted for a few passes, and banned for good
(never listened to again, from one scan to the next) after 3 listens in a row without speech. A
whitelisted frequency is never banned nor muted: it is captured as soon as it is above the threshold.
Interference is captured too (the 2.5 s), to judge whether it is a false positive.

After a capture with speech, the scan stays on the window and records the conversation until 20 s
pass without a transmission (recordings/ in the data directory, "Play recording" in the window).

"Join" pauses the scan (the dongle is freed) and opens GQRX on the frequency, in the right mode.
UI strings: lang/<lang>.sh next to the program. SIGUSR1 pauses the scan (so another app can take
the dongle).
"""
